course: dictionary
lesson: 1322
title: Caldera: a volcano's giant bowl
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe things you may never have seen. You can work out their meaning from the words around them, which are called the context. «When a huge eruption empties the magma chamber, the ground above can collapse into a giant crater called a caldera.» The clues are huge eruption, collapse and giant crater.
explain: The sentence says the ground collapses, so it falls inward and down, not up. A caldera must be a big dip or hollow, not a hill. Test your meaning in the sentence: «the ground above can collapse into a giant bowl-shaped hollow» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Science and geography lessons show calderas as giant craters, sometimes filled with water. Lake Taupō in New Zealand fills a caldera. When the context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Caldera» means a large bowl-shaped hollow formed when the top of a volcano collapses after a huge eruption.
fact: A caldera forms when the ground above an emptied magma chamber collapses.
fact: Some calderas fill with water and become lakes, such as Crater Lake in the USA and Lake Taupō in New Zealand.
fact: The Yellowstone caldera is a famous example shown in geography and science lessons.
exercise: «When a huge eruption empties the magma chamber, the ground above can collapse into a giant crater called a caldera.» What does caldera mean? | *A large bowl-shaped hollow left when a volcano's top collapses | A tall mountain that grows higher each year | A river of hot water under the ground | A small pond at the bottom of a hill
exercise: In a science lesson, a caldera is shown filled with water. What has formed? | A hill of rock | A cave under the sea | A forest of tall trees | *A lake
exercise: Find and copy one word from «the ground above can collapse into a giant crater» that means fall inward. | crater | giant | ground | *collapse
test: What happens to the ground above the magma chamber? | It rises up into a hill | *It collapses | It turns into water | It dances
test: Which country is Lake Taupō in, a lake that fills a caldera? | Canada | *New Zealand | Kenya | Scotland
exam: Which answer best explains what a caldera is? | *A giant bowl-shaped hollow left when a volcano's top collapses | A small hill made of soft sand | A type of fish that lives in lakes | A fast river that runs down a mountain
